<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92533" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίς</span></b> , ἡ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῑνός</span>, acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῖνα</span>, pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῖνες</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>nose</i> or <i>snout</i> of men and beasts, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.291
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.445
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.154
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				329d
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλκειν τινὰ τῆς
			ῥινός</span> lead him by the <i>nose</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				73
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλκεσθαι τῆς ῥ</span>.
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				68
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ τὴν χολὴν ἐπὶ ῥινὸς ἔχ᾽ εὐθύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					6.37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pl.
				<i>nostrils</i>, but freq., like Lat. <i>nares,
				nose</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.503
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.456
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				267
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				918
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				344
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα τε ῥῖνές τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.467
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				23.395
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				79e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> prob.
				<i>brow</i> of a hill or projecting <i>spur of land,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				14.352
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				 ii 36
			</span></i>, al. (<span class="entity">Halaesa</span>).—A later
			nom. form is <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίν</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.23
			</span></i> (prob. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῖνες</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				1.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; as name of a bandage, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				<u>Fasc.</u>
				11
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.418
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Trajan</span>).]</div>
